    "title": "Madison police arrest man on suspicion of fourth OWI offense - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Samantha Calderon ,\n11 hours ago MADISON, Wis. — A 58-year-old Madison man was arrested on the city's isthmus Monday afternoon on suspicion of his fourth operating while intoxicated offense, police said.\nAn officer stopped the driver on East Main Street near South Blount Street at around 2:35 p.m.\nPolice said the officer smelled intoxicants and saw open alcohol containers in the vehicle. The driver allegedly performed poorly on standard field sobriety tests and had a blood alcohol concentration above the legal limit.\nThe man also was arrested on suspicion of possessing open intoxicants, failing to install an ignition interlock device, operating with a prohibited blood alcohol concentration and operating after revocation.\nNews 3 Now is not naming the man at this time as part of a policy not to name people accused of crimes until they have been formally charged in court. Click here to learn more about the policy . He is currently being held in the Dane County Jail.\n​COPYRIGHT 2026 BY CHANNEL 3000. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. THIS MATERIAL MAY NOT BE PUBLISHED, BROADCAST, REWRITTEN OR REDISTRIBUTED.\n1",
